Ratio Spread & Box — Pricing and PNL Formula Reference
(Current Market Price, ATP, M2M, RLP, Net PnL — full working)

1. Core Principle (applies to every strategy below)
A multi-leg strategy doesn't have one single "market price" — it has a combo price built from each leg's live bid/ask, and this combo price is different depending on whether you're entering (buying) the structure or exiting (selling) it. This is because each individual leg has its own bid-ask spread, and those spreads stack up across legs.
The one rule that drives everything:
When you Buy something, you pay the Ask. When you Sell something, you receive the Bid.
Apply this leg-by-leg, then group by direction:
 ENTER the strategy now  =  Σ (Buy legs × Ask × lots)  −  Σ (Sell legs × Bid × lots)

Value if you EXIT the strategy now  =  Σ (Buy legs × Bid × lots)  −  Σ (Sell legs × Ask × lots)
    • Entry Cost → buy value 
    • Exit Value → this is what you'd actually get back today if you squared off a position you're already holding. 
    • The gap between these two numbers is the round-trip bid-ask cost of the whole structure — this is exactly why "unfavorable price fills" eat into PNL: the wider the individual leg spreads, the bigger this gap, the more it costs to get in and out. 
Everything below is just this same rule applied to specific strategy shapes.

2. Ratio 2 Leg
Structure: e.g. Buy 1 lot Option A (say ATM), Sell 2 lots Option B (say OTM) — ratio 1:2.
To BUY / Enter now:
Entry Cost = (Option_A_Ask × 1) − (Option_B_Bid × 2)
To SELL / Exit now (i.e. square off an existing position):
Exit Value = (Option_A_Bid × 1) − (Option_B_Ask × 2)
Worked example: Buy 1× 45500 CE, Sell 2× 44000 CE
Entry Cost = (45500_CE_Ask × 1) − (44000_CE_Bid × 2)
Exit Value = (45500_CE_Bid × 1) − (44000_CE_Ask × 2)

3. Ratio 3 Leg
Structure: 3 legs with a defined ratio, e.g. Buy 1 lot @ 45500, Sell 3 lots @ 44000, Buy 2 lots @ 42500.
To BUY / Enter now:
Entry Cost = (45500_Ask × 1) + (42500_Ask × 2) − (44000_Bid × 3)
(Both Buy legs grouped together and subtracted from the Sell leg's credit — Buy legs = cost, Sell leg = credit.)
To SELL / Exit now:
Exit Value = (45500_Bid × 1) + (42500_Bid × 2) − (44000_Ask × 3)
General rule reminder (from our earlier discussion): same-direction legs always get grouped together with the same sign. Two Buy legs → both negative in Entry Cost (both cost you money); never split one as + and one as − just because of leg order — the sign depends only on Buy vs Sell, never on leg position (1st/2nd/3rd).

4. Ratio 4 Leg
Structure: 4 legs, ratio e.g. r1:r2:r3:r4, each leg tagged Buy or Sell.
To BUY / Enter now:
Entry Cost = Σ (Buy legs: Ask × ratio_qty) − Σ (Sell legs: Bid × ratio_qty)
To SELL / Exit now:
Exit Value = Σ (Buy legs: Bid × ratio_qty) − Σ (Sell legs: Ask × ratio_qty)
Same pattern as 2-leg and 3-leg — just more terms in each group. However many legs a strategy has, sort them into "Buy bucket" and "Sell bucket" first, then apply the formula.

5. Box Spread (4 legs: 2 Calls + 2 Puts, 2 strikes)
Structure (Long Box): K1 = lower strike, K2 = higher strike
    • Buy Call K1 
    • Sell Call K2 
    • Sell Put K1 
    • Buy Put K2 
To BUY / Enter now:
Entry Cost = (Call_K1_Ask + Put_K2_Ask) − (Call_K2_Bid + Put_K1_Bid)
To SELL / Exit now:
Exit Value = (Call_K1_Bid + Put_K2_Bid) − (Call_K2_Ask + Put_K1_Ask)
Worked example: K1=23500, K2=25000
Entry Cost = (Call_23500_Ask + Put_25000_Ask) − (Call_25000_Bid + Put_23500_Bid)
Exit Value = (Call_23500_Bid + Put_25000_Bid) − (Call_25000_Ask + Put_23500_Ask)
Box-specific arbitrage check
A box always settles at exactly (K2 − K1) at expiry, no matter where the underlying ends up — this is what makes it a pure arbitrage trade (zero directional risk). So the number that actually matters:
Box Arbitrage Edge = (K2 − K1) − Entry Cost
    • If Entry Cost < (K2 − K1) → positive edge → profitable arbitrage (you're buying the box cheaper than its guaranteed expiry value). 
    • If Entry Cost ≥ (K2 − K1) → no edge (or negative) → don't take the trade, or check for a bad fill. 
This is the exact check to run before confirming any box fill — ties directly to the "unfavorable price fills in box strategies" PNL issue.

6. ATP (Average Traded Price) — per leg
Once actual fills happen (not live bid/ask anymore, but your real traded prices), ATP is the quantity-weighted average of all fills for that leg:
ATP = Σ (fill_qty_i × fill_price_i)  /  Σ fill_qty_i
Example: Buy 1 lot @ 535, then 2 more lots @ 540
ATP = (1×535 + 2×540) / (1+2) = 1615 / 3 = 538.33
    • B-ATP = average price of the Buy leg's fills 
    • S-ATP = average price of the Sell leg's fills 
ATP is your actual cost basis — different from the live bid/ask formulas above, which are theoretical (what it would cost right now). ATP is what it actually cost you, once filled.

7. M2M (Mark-to-Market) — live, unrealized
M2M tells you how much profit/loss you're sitting on right now, based on current market price vs. your actual fill price (ATP), for the portion still open.
M2M (Buy side)  = (Current_LTP − B-ATP) × B-TrQ × lot_size
M2M (Sell side) = (S-ATP − Current_LTP) × S-TrQ × lot_size

M2M (position) = M2M(Buy side) + M2M(Sell side)
    • If you bought at 535 and it's now trading at 540 → you're up (540−535) × qty → positive M2M. 
    • If you sold at 540 and it's now trading at 535 → you're up (540−535) × qty → positive M2M. 
    • Recalculates on every tick since Current_LTP keeps changing — this is why M2M flickers red/green live. 
For a multi-leg strategy, total M2M = sum of each individual leg's M2M.

8. RLP (Realized P/L) — booked, locked-in
RLP is profit/loss from quantity that has already been squared off — i.e., both a matching buy and sell have actually happened and closed out. Unlike M2M, this does not move with the market anymore.
RLP = Σ [ (Sell_price − Buy_price) × squared_off_qty ]   across all closed portions
Example: Bought 1 lot @ 535, later sold that same 1 lot @ 545 (squared off)
RLP = (545 − 535) × 1 = 10 × lot_size
This 10-point profit is now locked in — it won't change no matter what the market does afterward.

9. Net P/L
Simply the total of what's booked plus what's still open:
Net P/L = RLP + M2M
    • RLP = money already made/lost, locked in 
    • M2M = money currently being made/lost on what's still open, will keep moving until you exit 

10. Cut P/L (bonus — "what if I exit everything right now")
Treats the entire open position as if it were squared off instantly at current market (ignores slippage/spread, so it's slightly optimistic vs. reality):
Cut P/L = RLP + [ (Current_LTP − ATP) × Total_Open_Qty × direction ]
Compare this to Exit Value (Section 1/2/3/4/5 formulas) — Cut P/L uses LTP (single traded price, optimistic), while Exit Value uses actual Bid/Ask (realistic, accounts for spread cost). Exit Value is the more honest number for decision-making; Cut P/L is a quick single-number estimate.

11. Full Worked Example — Ratio 3 Leg, start to finish
Setup: Buy 1 lot 45500 CE, Sell 3 lots 44000 CE, Buy 2 lots 42500 CE
Step 1 — Check Entry Cost before placing (live bid/ask):
Entry Cost = (45500_Ask × 1) + (42500_Ask × 2) − (44000_Bid × 3)
→ If this looks favorable, place the order.
Step 2 — Order fills, now you have actual ATP:
B-ATP(45500 leg) = actual average fill price for that leg
B-ATP(42500 leg) = actual average fill price for that leg
S-ATP(44000 leg) = actual average fill price for that leg
Step 3 — While position is open, M2M updates live every tick:
M2M(45500 leg) = (Current_LTP_45500 − B-ATP_45500) × 1 × lot_size
M2M(42500 leg) = (Current_LTP_42500 − B-ATP_42500) × 2 × lot_size
M2M(44000 leg) = (S-ATP_44000 − Current_LTP_44000) × 3 × lot_size

Total M2M = sum of all three
Step 4 — You decide to exit. Check Exit Value (live bid/ask) first:
Exit Value = (45500_Bid × 1) + (42500_Bid × 2) − (44000_Ask × 3)
Step 5 — Once exit fills happen, that quantity moves from M2M into RLP:
RLP(45500 leg) = (Exit_fill_price − B-ATP_45500) × 1 × lot_size
RLP(42500 leg) = (Exit_fill_price − B-ATP_42500) × 2 × lot_size
RLP(44000 leg) = (S-ATP_44000 − Exit_fill_price) × 3 × lot_size

Total RLP = sum of all three
Step 6 — Final Net P/L for the trade:
Net P/L = Total RLP   (since M2M = 0 now, position fully closed)

12. Quick Reference Table
What you want to know
Formula
Cost to enter now (any strategy)
Σ(Buy legs × Ask) − Σ(Sell legs × Bid)
Value if exit now (any strategy)
Σ(Buy legs × Bid) − Σ(Sell legs × Ask)
Box arbitrage edge
(K2 − K1) − Entry Cost
ATP (per leg)
Σ(fill_qty × fill_price) / Σfill_qty
M2M (per leg)
(LTP − ATP) × Buy_Qty, or (ATP − LTP) × Sell_Qty
RLP (per leg, on close)
(Exit_price − ATP) × closed_qty, sign per direction
Net P/L
RLP + M2M
Cut P/L
RLP + (LTP − ATP) × Open_Qty (single-price estimate)


